"Prominence removal LANDED (commit b9cdcb7): server has no EntityProminenceComponent, no generate_prominence, no per-tick prominence system, no blob field; client derives EntityPresentation flags (hasPath/isPlayerControlled/hasHp) from already-subscribed tables and sorts locally. Bonus: one less public table streamed + one less per-tick full-table rewrite. NEW DESIGN QUESTIONS (2026-08-11, user): (a) In the threat view, should ACTION selection come FIRST, target(s) second? Motivated by future multi-target actions (simultaneous different attacks, attack+buff combos) where one action needs several targets with different purposes -- target-first cannot express 'this action needs two targets of different kinds'. (b) Split FOCUS from TARGET: today targeting doubles as examining an object's details; rename that examine role to focus and reserve target for action arguments -- with the ease-of-use exception that single-target attacks auto-target the current focus. Analysis pending user confirmation: action-first fits multi-target naturally (choose action -> it declares its target slots -> fill slots, with auto-fill from focus for single-slot attacks), while focus stays a pure inspection cursor that never fires anything by itself; server act() would eventually take a target LIST or per-slot arguments -- schema change to plan alongside the Activate action type."